o><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">0</mn></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">A</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span></li>\n<li>Show that the second minimum really does range over strictly more\nsubspaces, by exhibiting a one-dimensional subspace of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{C}^2\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2102 TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">C</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> that contains no nonzero real\nvector.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch17-variational/02-courant-fischer.html"}